  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Performance\n\n- Removing or inserting a registration no longer rebuilds the imposters after it (#440, closes #408). The driver compares registered targets by position, so removing or inserting one [assembly: GenerateImposter(...)] regenerated every imposter registered after it, even though none of them changed. The generator now reuses a source when its target and C# version haven't changed. In a project with 20 targets of 30 members each, removing the first registration now takes 4 ms in the generator, down from 477 ms. The generated code is unchanged.\n- Method Throws setups allocate one closure instead of two (#441, closes #437). The setup step wrapped the builder's throwing lambda in a second one. It now uses that lambda directly. Per setup:\n\n  | Setup | 1.0.8 | 1.0.9 |\n  | --- | ---: | ---: |\n  | Throws(exception) | 472 B | 384 B |\n  | Throws(_ => exception) | 472 B | 384 B |\n  | Throws<InvalidOperationException>() | 384 B | 296 B |\n\n  Throws<TException>() captures nothing, so its setup no longer allocates any closure.",
